     Devprc                    PROGRAMMER UTILITY                    Devprc     NNAAMMEE               Devprc - show which device belongs to which process(es)      SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS               devprc [-a] [[-d <device>] [-h]]     DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN               devprc  displays  tables  showing which device is associated with          which process.  the following options are recognized:           -a      all devices (default)                   a listing of all processes and devices is produced.                    this listing consists of:                      PID         - process id                      NAME        - process name                      PROCESSPATH - the program path no. ,i.e:                                     0 = stdin                                     1 = stdout                                     3 = stderr etc.                       SYSPATH     - the system (kernel) path no.                       DEVICE      - the device name                      FILENAME    - if the device is an RBF-device,                                     the filename is shown           -d      show processes associated with one device.                    this option needs the devicename as a parameter.                    its primary purpose is to get the no.'s of running                   processes for killing them in shell scripts to free                   up the associated devices.                    the output consists of a number (process id) in the                   first column followed by a tab (0x09) and the process                   name.            -h      this option is only possible with the -d option. its                   purpose is to write a header prior to the output                    described under the -d option.       Page 1                                  Printed (10 Mae 1990 13:16:22)